  "content": {
    "id": "p4-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Do you think the following statements are true or false for all values of $x$? If you think a statement is false, provide a specific value of $x$ showing this.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p4-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$|x-3|=|3-x|$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "$$|3-x|=|-(x-3)|=|x-3|.$$\nAn expression and its negative have the same absolute value.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$|x-1|=1-x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False; for example, $x=2$.",
          "worked": "At $x=2$,\n$$\\begin{align*}|x-1|&=|2-1|=1\\\\1-x&=1-2=-1.\\end{align*}$$\nThe two sides are unequal.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q9-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$|5x|=5|x|$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "$$|5x|=|5||x|=5|x|.$$\nAbsolute value is multiplicative.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q9-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$|x|^2=x^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "For $x\\geq0$, $|x|^2=x^2$. For $x<0$, $|x|^2=(-x)^2=x^2$. Thus the statement holds for every real $x$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q9-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$|-3x|=3x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False; for example, $x=-1$.",
          "worked": "At $x=-1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}|-3x|&=|-3(-1)|=3\\\\3x&=3(-1)=-3.\\end{align*}$$\nThe two sides are unequal.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q9-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\sqrt{x^2}=x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False; for example, $x=-1$.",
          "worked": "At $x=-1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{x^2}&=\\sqrt{(-1)^2}=1\\\\x&=-1.\\end{align*}$$\nThe two sides are unequal. In general, $\\sqrt{x^2}=|x|$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      }
    ]
  },
